  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<math> <mrow> <mtext>A</mtext><mover> <mo>→</mo> <mrow> <mtext>burns,</mtext><mtext> </mtext><mtext>nitrogen</mtext></mrow> </mover> <munder> <mtext>B</mtext> <mrow> <mtext>ionic</mtext><mtext> </mtext><mtext>compound</mtext></mrow> </munder> <mover> <mo>→</mo> <mrow> <msub> <mtext>H</mtext> <mtext>2</mtext> </msub> <mtext>O</mtext></mrow> </mover> <munder> <mtext>C</mtext> <mrow> <mtext>milky</mtext><mtext> </mtext><mtext>solution</mtext></mrow> </munder> <mtext> </mtext><mtext>+</mtext><mtext> </mtext><mtext>D</mtext><mover> <mo>→</mo> <mrow> <msub> <mrow> <mtext>CO</mtext></mrow> <mtext>2</mtext> </msub> </mrow> </mover> </mrow> </math><br />Since the solution of C becomes milky on bubbling <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> into it, C is lime water <math><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><msub><mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfenced><mo>.</mo></math> Thus, the element A is calcium and B is the compound of calcium with nitrogen. Nitrides on reacting with water give the corresponding hydroxide and ammonia. Therefore,<br />A is calcium (Ca)<br />B is calcium nitride <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfenced></math> .<br />C is lime water <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><msub><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math><br />D is ammonia <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfenced></math> .<br /><math> <mrow> <mtext>Ca</mtext><mover> <mo>→</mo> <mrow> <mtext>burns,</mtext><mtext> </mtext><mtext>nitrogen</mtext></mrow> </mover> <munder> <mrow> <msub> <mrow> <mtext>Ca</mtext></mrow> <mn>3</mn> </msub> <msub> <mtext>N</mtext> <mn>2</mn> </msub> </mrow> <mrow> <mtext>ionic</mtext><mtext> </mtext><mtext>compound</mtext></mrow> </munder> <mover> <mo>→</mo> <mrow> <msub> <mtext>H</mtext> <mn>2</mn> </msub> <mtext>O</mtext></mrow> </mover> <munder> <mrow> <mtext>Ca</mtext><msub> <mrow> <mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mtext>OH</mtext><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow> <mn>2</mn> </msub> </mrow> <mrow> <mtext>milky</mtext><mtext> </mtext><mtext>solution</mtext></mrow> </munder> <mtext> </mtext><mo>+</mo><mtext> </mtext><msub> <mrow> <mtext>NH</mtext></mrow> <mn>3</mn> </msub> <mover> <mo>→</mo> <mrow> <msub> <mrow> <mtext>CO</mtext></mrow> <mn>2</mn> </msub> </mrow> </mover> <msub> <mrow> <mtext>CaCO</mtext></mrow> <mn>3</mn> </msub> </mrow> </math>",
